# bootstrap/CHAIN - the seed lineage, one row per committed seed, in
# history order. Read by scripts/check-seed-lineage.sh, which replays
# every row under --full, and on a default run the rows that
# bootstrap/CHAIN.checkpoint does not certify - never fewer than the
# last one. That checkpoint carries the digest of the prefix it covers
# and the gate recomputes it from THIS file on every run, so a row
# inside the covered prefix that moves by one byte voids it and the
# whole chain is replayed. Written by scripts/reseed.sh, which appends
# a row for each seed it generates; a reseed only appends, so it never
# voids the checkpoint.
#
#   <seed> <from> <method> <matched> <seconds> [skips=<orphan>] [list=<file>] [prior=<seed>]
#
#   seed      the commit that wrote the seed - or `next`, the seed now in
#             the tree whose commit did not exist when the row was
#             written (the gate resolves it to the last commit that
#             wrote bootstrap/*.ll)
#   from      the seed it reproduces from: the row before it, or the
#             Rust anchor bb730db for the first row
#   method    rust-anchor  cargo builds the Rust compiler at bb730db, it
#                          compiles this seed's tree into stage1, and
#                          stage1's emission is this seed
#             seed         the previous seed compiles this seed's tree;
#                          that emission, or its own re-emission, is
#                          this seed
#             mixed-tree   the previous seed cannot compile this tree
#                          (asserted) but compiles self_host@this over
#                          stdlib@previous into an intermediate that can
#             skip         `seed`, over an orphan between the two that the
#                          same replay shows not to be its tree's emission
#             walk         every source commit between the two, each
#                          compiled by the compiler built from the one
#                          before, from the file `list=` names
#             restore      the commit copied an earlier row's whole
#                          bootstrap/ tree, byte for byte, back into place;
#                          `prior=` names that row, `matched` is - and
#                          seconds 0, because nothing is compiled
#             bridge-needed  written by reseed.sh --bridge: the seed was
#                          generated by a compiler that is not the previous
#                          seed's descendant, and the gate is red until the
#                          row is replaced by one that replays
#   matched   which emission equalled the seed: stage1 is the previous
#             compiler's emission of the tree, stage2 that emission's
#             own re-emission (for the anchor and mixed-tree, stage1 is
#             the intermediate and stage2 its emission)
#   seconds   the replay's measured time on the machine that wrote the row
#
# Seeds compare byte for byte, except that the directory inside an
# `; axiom-asm-file N "PATH"` comment is read as `<stdlib>`: compilers
# before b81ceef3 wrote the build machine's directory there, and the
# compiler has written `<stdlib>` itself since.
#
# An `orphan` line names a commit that wrote the seed but whose seed is
# NOT its tree's emission - it was generated by a compiler built from an
# uncommitted tree, before reseed.sh generated from the committed seed -
# and so has no row: it is bypassed, and the row after it says how.
# bootstrap/README.md states the gap in prose.
#
# Measured 2026-08-29 on darwin-aarch64 (Homebrew LLVM 23.1.0, cargo
# 1.97.1). Every row was replayed by the gate in the session that wrote
# it; a row nobody replayed is not written.

